From 73ba5e75cc53fb4277a0b284aa060c45fbc5a0aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:54:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] One slip can carry several contracts (delivery parts)

A truck load that carries two contracts is now one slip: the main
delivery row keeps the slip money, uang tembak and stage; each extra
contract is its own delivery row on its own contract (own DO number,
muatan/bongkar) linked by parent_id. Contract totals are unchanged;
trips, uang tembak, route km and the fleet overview fold parts into
their slip.

- 0037_delivery_parts.sql: parent_id (cascade), one-level/sync
  triggers, unique (parent_id, contract_id), no money on parts
- Slip page: "+ Kontrak", second contract on new slips, estimate
  split, print both contracts, DO renumbered on contract change
- Contract page: part/slip badges, shared fields read-only on parts
- Tembak, route history, daily report, fleet overview: per trip

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WPA1AR2Ga5HUjU8QoMMudG
